var documenterSearchIndex = {"docs":
[{"category":"section","location":"internals/mesh/#Mesh","page":"Mesh","text":"","title":"Mesh"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-Reference","page":"API Reference","text":"Documentation for Bramble.jl's public API.\n\n","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Utilities","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Utilities"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Linear-Algebra-Backends","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Linear Algebra Backends"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Function-Embedding","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Function Embedding"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Geometry","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Geometry"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Sets-and-Intervals-(CartesianProduct)","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Sets and Intervals (CartesianProduct)"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Markers-and-Domains","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Markers and Domains"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.backend","page":"API Reference","text":"backend(; vector_type, matrix_type)\n\n\nCreates a linear algebra Backend using keyword arguments.\n\nDefaults to standard dense Float64 vectors and SparseMatrixCSC matrices:\n\nvector_type = Vector{Float64}\nmatrix_type = SparseMatrixCSC{Float64,Int}\n\nExamples\n\njulia> dense_sparse = backend() # Default backend (Dense-Sparse Float64)\n\njulia> using SparseArrays;\n       SVec{T} = SparseVector{T,Int};\n       SMat{T} = SparseMatrixCSC{T,Int};\n       T64 = Float64;\n\njulia> sparse_sparse = backend(vector_type = SVec{T64}, matrix_type = SMat{T64})\n\njulia> T32 = Float32;\n       dense32 = backend(vector_type = Vector{T32}, matrix_type = SMat{T32})\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.backend"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.vector","page":"API Reference","text":"vector(_, n)\n\n\nCreates a vector of type VT associated with the given Backend instance with length n.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.vector"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.matrix","page":"API Reference","text":"matrix(backend, n, m)\n\n\nCreates a matrix of type MT associated with the given Backend instance with dimensions n × m.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.matrix"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.vector_type","page":"API Reference","text":"vector_type(_)\n\n\nReturns the vector type (VT) associated with the given Backend instance or type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.vector_type"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.matrix_type","page":"API Reference","text":"matrix_type(_)\n\n\nReturns the matrix type (MT) associated with the given Backend instance or type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.matrix_type"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.backend_types","page":"API Reference","text":"backend_types(backend)\n\n\nReturns a tuple with the backend associated types:\n\nElement type of VT\nVector type VT\nMatrix type MT\nConcrete backend type Backend{VT,MT}\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.backend_types"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.backend_eye","page":"API Reference","text":"backend_eye(backend, n)\n\n\nConstructs an n × n identity matrix associated with the given Backend instance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.backend_eye"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.backend_zeros","page":"API Reference","text":"backend_zeros(backend, n)\n\n\nConstructs an n × n zero matrix associated with the given Backend instance.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.backend_zeros"},{"category":"type","location":"api/#Bramble.BrambleFunction","page":"API Reference","text":"struct BrambleFunction{ArgsType, hastime, CoType, DType}\n\nInternal structure wrapping user-defined functions for type-agnostic, zero-overhead dispatch.\nUses FunctionWrappers.FunctionWrapper to provide stable, compiled calling signatures.\n\nFields\n\nwrapped: A FunctionWrapper wrapper for the function\ndomain: Domain of the function (typically a CartesianProduct or Domain)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.BrambleFunction"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.embed_function","page":"API Reference","text":"embed_function(space_domain, func)\n\n\nEmbeds a Julia function into a BrambleFunction defined over space_domain (and optional time_domain).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.embed_function"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.has_time","page":"API Reference","text":"has_time(_)\n\n\nChecks if a BrambleFunction is time-dependent by inspecting its hastime type parameter.\nReturns true if time-dependent, false otherwise.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.has_time"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.interval","page":"API Reference","text":"interval(x, y)\n\n\nConstructs a 1-dimensional CartesianProduct representing the closed interval x y.\nInputs are converted to floating-point numbers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.interval"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.point","page":"API Reference","text":"point(x)\n\n\nCreates a collapsed 1D CartesianProduct representing the point x x.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.point"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.box","page":"API Reference","text":"box(a, b)\n\n\nCreates a CartesianProduct from two points a and b, defining opposite corners of the bounding box.\nIntervals are constructed as min(a_i b_i) max(a_i b_i).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.box"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.cartesian_product","page":"API Reference","text":"cartesian_product(x, y)\n\n\nReturns a CartesianProduct from coordinates or intervals.\n\nIf two scalar values x and y are provided, returns a 1D CartesianProduct representing x y.\nIf an NTuple{D, Tuple{T,T}} is provided, returns a D-dimensional CartesianProduct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.cartesian_product"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.:×","page":"API Reference","text":"×(X::CartesianProduct, Y::CartesianProduct)\n\nComputes the tensor product of two CartesianProducts X and Y.\nThe resulting dimension is dim(X) + dim(Y) with promoted element type.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.:×"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.dim","page":"API Reference","text":"dim(_)\n\n\nReturns the spatial dimension D where the CartesianProduct is embedded.\n\n\n\n\n\ndim(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the dimension of the space where the Domain Ω is embedded.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.dim"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.topo_dim","page":"API Reference","text":"topo_dim(X)\n\n\nReturns the topological dimension of a CartesianProduct (embedded dimension minus collapsed dimensions).\n\n\n\n\n\ntopo_dim(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the topological dimension of Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.topo_dim"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.tails","page":"API Reference","text":"tails(X, i)\n\n\nReturns the i-th component interval of CartesianProduct X as a Tuple{T,T}. Alias for X(i).\n\n\n\n\n\ntails(X)\n\n\nReturns the component sets of a CartesianProduct:\n\nfor a 1D product (D=1), returns the single interval tuple (min, max).\nfor a D-dimensional product, returns an NTuple{D, Tuple{T,T}} of all component intervals.\n\n\n\n\n\ntails(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the boundary tails/intervals of the underlying set of Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.tails"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.center","page":"API Reference","text":"center(cp)\n\n\nReturns the center point of a CartesianProduct domain as an SVector{D,T}.\n\n\n\n\n\ncenter(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the center point of Domain Ω as an SVector{D,T}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.center"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.projection","page":"API Reference","text":"projection(X, i)\n\n\nReturns the i-th component interval of X as a new 1D CartesianProduct.\n\n\n\n\n\nprojection(Ω, i)\n\n\nReturns the i-th 1D CartesianProduct component of the set associated with Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.projection"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.is_collapsed","page":"API Reference","text":"Checks if a 1D CartesianProduct or two numbers are \"collapsed\" (i.e., degenerate).\n\nFor two numbers a and b, returns true if isapprox(a, b).\nFor a 1-dimensional CartesianProduct, returns X.collapsed[1].\n\n\n\n\n\nis_collapsed(Ω)\n\n\nReturns whether the underlying set of Domain Ω is collapsed.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.is_collapsed"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.point_type","page":"API Reference","text":"point_type(_)\n\n\nDetermines the coordinate point type within a CartesianProduct space.\nReturns T for 1D spaces and NTuple{D,T} for D-dimensional spaces.\n\n\n\n\n\npoint_type(Ω)\n\n\nDetermines the coordinate point type within a Domain space.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.point_type"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.get_boundary_symbols","page":"API Reference","text":"get_boundary_symbols(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a tuple of default boundary symbols for a CartesianProduct or Domain.\n\n1D x_1 x_2: (:left, :right)\n2D x_1 x_2 times y_1 y_2: (:bottom, :top, :left, :right)\n3D x_1 x_2 times y_1 y_2 times z_1 z_2: (:bottom, :top, :back, :front, :left, :right)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.get_boundary_symbols"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.set","page":"API Reference","text":"set(X)\n\n\nReturns the CartesianProduct itself (identity operation).\n\n\n\n\n\nset(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the CartesianProduct geometric set associated with the Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.set"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.markers","page":"API Reference","text":"markers(space_set, pairs)\n\n\nConstructs a DomainMarkers object from a series of label => identifier pairs.\n\nThe identifier can be a Symbol, a Tuple of Symbols, or a Function.\n\nExample\n\njulia> I = cartesian_product(0.0, 1.0);\njulia> m = markers(I, :left_boundary => :left, :internal => x -> 0.2 < x < 0.8);\njulia> length(m.symbols)\n1\njulia> length(m.conditions)\n1\n\n\n\n\n\nmarkers(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the DomainMarkers object associated with the Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.markers"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.domain","page":"API Reference","text":"domain(X)\n\n\nReturns a Domain from a CartesianProduct.\n\ndomain(X): Assumes a default :boundary marker covering all boundaries of X.\ndomain(X, markers::DomainMarkers): Constructs a domain with explicit markers.\ndomain(X, pairs...): Constructs a domain with markers defined by label-identifier pairs.\ndomain(space_set, time_set, pairs...): Constructs a spatio-temporal domain.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.domain"},{"category":"function","location":"api/#Bramble.labels","page":"API Reference","text":"labels(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a generator that yields the labels (Symbol) of all markers associated with the Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.labels"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/form/#Forms","page":"Forms","text":"","title":"Forms"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/geometry/#Geometry","page":"Geometry","text":"","title":"Geometry"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/geometry/#Sets","page":"Geometry","text":"","title":"Sets"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/geometry/#Markers","page":"Geometry","text":"","title":"Markers"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/geometry/#Domains","page":"Geometry","text":"","title":"Domains"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.CartesianProduct","page":"Geometry","text":"struct CartesianProduct{D, T}\n\nA type representing the Cartesian product of D closed intervals in a space with element type T.\n\nFields\n\nbox: a container of D pairs, where each pair represents the bounds (min, max) of an interval\ncollapsed: a container of D boolean values indicating whether each dimension is collapsed (i.e., min = max)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.CartesianProduct"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.CartesianProduct-Union{Tuple{Integer}, Tuple{D}} where D","page":"Geometry","text":"(X::CartesianProduct)(i)\n\nReturns the i-th interval (or point bounds) in the CartesianProduct as a Tuple{T,T}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.CartesianProduct"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.eltype-Union{Tuple{Bramble.CartesianProduct{D, T}}, Tuple{T}, Tuple{D}} where {D, T}","page":"Geometry","text":"eltype(_)\n\n\nReturns the coordinate element type T of a CartesianProduct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.eltype"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.first-Tuple{Bramble.CartesianProduct{1}}","page":"Geometry","text":"first(X)\n\n\nReturn the lower (first) and upper (last) bounds of a one-dimensional CartesianProduct.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.first"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.in-Tuple{Number, Bramble.CartesianProduct{1}}","page":"Geometry","text":"Base.in(x, X::CartesianProduct)\n\nReturns true if point x is contained in the closed CartesianProduct domain.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.in"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.show-Union{Tuple{T}, Tuple{D}, Tuple{IO, Bramble.CartesianProduct{D, T}}} where {D, T}","page":"Geometry","text":"Base.show(io::IO, X::CartesianProduct)\n\nCustom display for CartesianProduct objects, showing dimension information, bounds, and collapsed status with colors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.show"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.DomainMarkers","page":"Geometry","text":"struct DomainMarkers{BFType}\n\nA container that categorizes and stores all markers for a given computational domain.\n\nFields\n\nsymbols: markers identified by a single predefined Symbol (e.g., :left).\ntuples: markers identified by a collection of predefined Symbols (e.g., (:top, :right)).\nconditions: markers identified by a boolean function f(x) or f(x, t).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.DomainMarkers"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.DomainMarkers-Tuple{Number}","page":"Geometry","text":"(dm::DomainMarkers)(t::Number)\n\nEvaluates a time-dependent DomainMarkers object at a specific time t.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.DomainMarkers"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.EvaluatedDomainMarkers","page":"Geometry","text":"struct EvaluatedDomainMarkers{M<:Bramble.DomainMarkers, T<:Number}\n\nA lazy, view-like wrapper representing a DomainMarkers object evaluated at a specific time t.\n\nFields\n\noriginal_markers: the original time-dependent DomainMarkers instance.\nevaluation_time: the evaluation timestamp.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.EvaluatedDomainMarkers"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.Marker","page":"Geometry","text":"struct Marker{F}\n\nRepresents a labeled region or boundary of a computational domain.\n\nEach Marker consists of a label (a Symbol) and an identifier. The identifier specifies how to locate the marked region:\n\nA Symbol for predefined boundaries (e.g., :left, :top).\nA Set{Symbol} for collections of predefined boundaries (e.g., Set([:top, :right])).\nA function (wrapped in a BrambleFunction) that acts as a characteristic or level-set function returning true for points in the marked region.\n\nFields\n\nlabel: A Symbol naming the marked region (e.g., :inlet, :wall, :boundary).\nidentifier: The object identifying the region (Symbol, Set{Symbol}, or BrambleFunction).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.Marker"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.MarkerPair","page":"Geometry","text":"MarkerPair{F}\n\nA type alias for Pair{Symbol, F}, representing a convenient way to define a marker (e.g., :boundary => :left).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.MarkerPair"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.isempty-Tuple{Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"Base.isempty(dm::DomainMarkers)\n\nChecks if a DomainMarkers object contains zero markers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.isempty"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.length-Tuple{Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"Base.length(dm::DomainMarkers)\n\nReturns the total number of markers in a DomainMarkers object.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.length"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.show-Tuple{IO, Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"Base.show(io::IO, dm::DomainMarkers)\n\nCustom display for DomainMarkers objects with colored formatting.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.show"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.show-Union{Tuple{F}, Tuple{IO, Bramble.Marker{F}}} where F","page":"Geometry","text":"Base.show(io::IO, m::Marker)\n\nCustom display for Marker objects.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.show"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.conditions-Tuple{Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"conditions(domain_markers)\n\n\nReturns the set of function condition markers from a DomainMarkers object.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.conditions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.conditions-Tuple{Bramble.EvaluatedDomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"conditions(edm)\n\n\nReturns a lazy generator that yields time-evaluated markers at edm.evaluation_time.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.conditions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.identifier-Tuple{Bramble.Marker}","page":"Geometry","text":"identifier(m)\n\n\nReturns the identifier (Symbol, Set{Symbol}, or function) of a Marker or MarkerPair.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.identifier"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.label-Tuple{Bramble.Marker}","page":"Geometry","text":"label(m)\n\n\nReturns the Symbol label of a Marker or MarkerPair.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.label"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.label_conditions-Tuple{Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"label_conditions(domain_markers)\n\n\nReturns a generator that yields the labels from the function-based condition markers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.label_conditions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.label_identifiers-Tuple{Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"label_identifiers(domain_markers)\n\n\nReturns a generator that yields the label (Symbol) of every marker in the DomainMarkers collection.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.label_identifiers"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.label_symbols-Tuple{Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"label_symbols(domain_markers)\n\n\nReturns a generator that yields the labels from the single-symbol markers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.label_symbols"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.label_tuples-Tuple{Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"label_tuples(domain_markers)\n\n\nReturns a generator that yields the labels from the symbol-tuple markers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.label_tuples"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.symbols-Tuple{Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"symbols(domain_markers)\n\n\nReturns the set of single-symbol markers from a DomainMarkers object.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.symbols"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.tuples-Tuple{Bramble.DomainMarkers}","page":"Geometry","text":"tuples(domain_markers)\n\n\nReturns the set of symbol-tuple markers from a DomainMarkers object.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.tuples"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.Domain","page":"Geometry","text":"struct Domain{SetType, MarkersType} <: Bramble.DomainBaseType\n\nRepresents a computational domain, combining a geometric set (e.g., CartesianProduct) with a collection of labeled DomainMarkers.\n\nFields\n\nset: the geometric set defining the domain's extent (e.g., a CartesianProduct).\nmarkers: a DomainMarkers object containing all labeled regions for this domain.\n\nRelated Types\n\nUse mesh to discretize a Domain into a computational mesh.\nSee CartesianProduct for the underlying geometric representation.\nSee DomainMarkers for marker management.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.Domain"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.Domain-Tuple{Number}","page":"Geometry","text":"(Ω::Domain)(t::Number)\n\nEvaluates a time-dependent Domain at time t, returning a time-evaluated Domain.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.Domain"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.eltype-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"eltype(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the element type of the bounds defining Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.eltype"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.in-Tuple{Any, Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"Base.in(x, Ω::Domain)\n\nReturns true if point x is contained in the closed Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.in"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.isempty-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"isempty(Ω)\n\n\nReturns true if Domain Ω has no markers attached.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.isempty"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.length-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"length(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the total number of markers defined on Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.length"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Base.show-Tuple{IO, Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"Base.show(io::IO, Ω::Domain)\n\nCustom display for Domain objects, combining set geometry and marker information with colors.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.show"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.conditions-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"conditions(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the set of condition-based markers associated with the Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.conditions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.label_conditions-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"label_conditions(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a generator with the labels of function condition markers on Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.label_conditions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.label_identifiers-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"label_identifiers(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a generator with all marker labels on Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.label_identifiers"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.label_symbols-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"label_symbols(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a generator with the labels of symbol markers on Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.label_symbols"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.label_tuples-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"label_tuples(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a generator with the labels of symbol-tuple markers on Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.label_tuples"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.marker_conditions-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"marker_conditions(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a generator yielding the identifiers (functions) of condition-based markers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.marker_conditions"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.marker_identifiers-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"marker_identifiers(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a generator that yields the identifiers (Symbol, Set{Symbol}, or BrambleFunction) of all markers in the Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.marker_identifiers"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.marker_symbols-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"marker_symbols(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a generator yielding the identifiers of single-symbol markers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.marker_symbols"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.marker_tuples-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"marker_tuples(Ω)\n\n\nReturns a generator yielding the identifiers of symbol-tuple markers.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.marker_tuples"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.symbols-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"symbols(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the set of single-symbol markers associated with the Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.symbols"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/geometry/#Bramble.tuples-Tuple{Bramble.Domain}","page":"Geometry","text":"tuples(Ω)\n\n\nReturns the set of symbol-tuple markers associated with the Domain Ω.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.tuples"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/space/#Spaces","page":"Spaces","text":"","title":"Spaces"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/utils/#Utilities","page":"Utilities","text":"","title":"Utilities"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/utils/#Backend","page":"Utilities","text":"","title":"Backend"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/utils/#Linear-Algebra","page":"Utilities","text":"","title":"Linear Algebra"},{"category":"section","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble-Function","page":"Utilities","text":"","title":"Bramble Function"},{"category":"type","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble.Backend","page":"Utilities","text":"struct Backend{VT<:(AbstractVector), MT<:(AbstractMatrix)}\n\nA singleton structure containing type-level configuration for backend linear algebra objects.\nThis structure has no fields, only type parameters VT and MT.\n\nThis allows specifying the desired concrete types for vectors and matrices\n(e.g., dense Vector, sparse SparseVector, different element types like\nFloat32, Float64, or custom GPU arrays).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.Backend"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Base.eltype-Union{Tuple{Bramble.Backend{VT, MT}}, Tuple{MT}, Tuple{VT}} where {VT, MT}","page":"Utilities","text":"eltype(backend)\n\n\nReturns the coordinate/element type of the vector type (VT) used in the given Backend.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Base.eltype"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble._dot-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractVector, AbstractVector}","page":"Utilities","text":"_dot(u, v, w)\n\n\nComputes the weighted element-wise dot product of three vectors:\nsum_i u_i cdot v_i cdot w_i\n\nUses SIMD and fused multiply-add operations for maximal performance without allocations.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble._dot"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble._inner_product-Tuple{AbstractVector, AbstractVector, AbstractVector}","page":"Utilities","text":"_inner_product(u, h, v)\n\n\nComputes the weighted inner product langle u v rangle_h.\n\nFor vectors u and v with weights h, computes sum_i u_i h_i v_i via _dot.\nFor matrices u and v, computes v^T operatornamediag(h) u.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble._inner_product"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble._parallel_for!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Utilities","text":"_parallel_for!(v, idxs, f)\n\n\nParallel implementation of a for-loop that modifies array v in-place using static thread scheduling.\n\nArguments\n\nv: Array to be modified in-place\nidxs: Iterable of indices to process\nf: Function that takes an index and returns the value to be stored at that index\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble._parallel_for!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble._serial_for!-Tuple{Any, Any, Any}","page":"Utilities","text":"_serial_for!(v, idxs, f)\n\n\nPerforms a serial (single-threaded) iteration over the specified indices, applying a function f to modify array v in-place.\n\nArguments\n\nv: Array to be modified in-place\nidxs: Indices to iterate over\nf: Function to be applied at each index\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble._serial_for!"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble._embed_notime-Tuple{Any, Any}","page":"Utilities","text":"_embed_notime(X, f; CoType)\n\n\nCreates a time-independent (hastime=false) BrambleFunction.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble._embed_notime"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble._embed_withtime-Tuple{Any, Bramble.CartesianProduct{1}, Any}","page":"Utilities","text":"_embed_withtime(space_domain, time_domain, f; FinalCoType)\n\n\nEmbeds a time-dependent function f(x, t) over spatial domain space_domain and 1D time domain time_domain.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble._embed_withtime"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble._get_args_type-Union{Tuple{Bramble.CartesianProduct{1, T}}, Tuple{T}} where T","page":"Utilities","text":"_get_args_type(_)\n_get_args_type(X)\n\n\nInternal helper to determine the expected argument type for a function based on domain X.\n\nIf the domain is 1D: returns scalar element type T.\nIf the domain is D-dimensional: returns NTuple{D, T}.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble._get_args_type"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble._get_domains-Tuple{Any}","page":"Utilities","text":"_get_domains(domain_spec)\n\n\nParses a domain specification into (space_domain, time_domain).\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble._get_domains"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble.argstype-Union{Tuple{FunctionWrappers.FunctionWrapper{CoType, Tuple{ArgsType}}}, Tuple{ArgsType}, Tuple{CoType}} where {CoType, ArgsType}","page":"Utilities","text":"argstype(_)\n\n\nExtracts the argument type ArgsType from a FunctionWrapper.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.argstype"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble.bramble_function_with_domain-Tuple{Any, Any, Bool, Type}","page":"Utilities","text":"bramble_function_with_domain(f, X, hastime, CoType; domain)\n\n\nConstructs a BrambleFunction bundling function f with its domain X.\n\nArguments\n\nf: Function to wrap\nX: Spatial domain used to infer the argument type of f\nhastime: Boolean flag indicating time dependence\nCoType: Return type of function f\ndomain: Domain object to store in the struct (defaults to X)\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.bramble_function_with_domain"},{"category":"method","location":"internals/utils/#Bramble.codomaintype-Union{Tuple{FunctionWrappers.FunctionWrapper{CoType, Tuple{ArgsType}}}, Tuple{ArgsType}, Tuple{CoType}} where {CoType, ArgsType}","page":"Utilities","text":"codomaintype(_)\n\n\nExtracts the codomain type CoType from a FunctionWrapper.\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"Bramble.codomaintype"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#tutorial_geometry","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Bramble.jl provides a high-performance, zero-allocation geometric modeling subsystem designed for partial differential equations (PDEs) and numerical discretization schemes on Cartesian and tensor-product meshes.\n\nIn this tutorial, you will learn how to:\n\nConstruct 1D intervals and multi-dimensional CartesianProducts.\nHandle collapsed (lower-dimensional) geometries.\nQuery spatial and topological dimensions, bounds, centers, and containment.\nDefine boundary labels and markers with markers.\nBuild complete computational Domains ready for mesh generation and PDE solvers.\n\n","title":"Geometry Tutorial"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#1.-Sets-and-intervals","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"At the core of the geometry system is CartesianProduct{D, T}, which represents the Cartesian product of D closed intervals in mathbbR^D with coordinate type T.","title":"1. Sets and intervals"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#1.1-Creating-1D-intervals","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Use interval to define closed intervals a b subset mathbbR:\n\nusing Bramble\n\n# Define the interval [0.0, 1.0]\nI = interval(0.0, 1.0)\n\n# Automatic conversion of integer bounds to floating point\nI_int = interval(0, 2)  # CartesianProduct{1, Float64}\n\n# Create a single degenerate point [0.5, 0.5]\nP = point(0.5)\n\n# Bounding box of any two numbers (ordered automatically)\nB = box(1.5, 0.2)       # [0.2, 1.5]","title":"1.1 Creating 1D intervals"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#1.2-Multi-dimensional-sets-via-the-tensor-product-operator","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Multi-dimensional hyper-rectangles are constructed intuitively by taking the tensor product of lower-dimensional sets using the × (\\times<tab>) operator:\n\n# 2D Unit square: [0, 1] × [0, 1]\nΩ_2d = interval(0.0, 1.0) × interval(0.0, 1.0)\n\n# 3D Cuboid: [-1, 1] × [0, 2] × [0, 0.5]\nΩ_3d = interval(-1.0, 1.0) × interval(0.0, 2.0) × interval(0.0, 0.5)\n\nAlternatively, you can construct products directly using tuples of interval pairs:\n\n# Direct tuple construction\nΩ_2d = cartesian_product(((0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 2.0)))\n\n","title":"1.2 Multi-dimensional sets via the tensor product operator ×"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#2.-Querying-geometric-properties","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Bramble.jl provides a comprehensive, type-stable query interface:\n\nX = interval(0.0, 2.0) × interval(-1.0, 1.0)\n\n# Spatial embedding dimension (D = 2)\ndim(X)            # 2\n\n# Topological dimension\ntopo_dim(X)       # 2\n\n# Interval bounds\ntails(X)          # ((0.0, 2.0), (-1.0, 1.0))\ntails(X, 1)       # (0.0, 2.0)  -- bounds in dimension 1\ntails(X, 2)       # (-1.0, 1.0) -- bounds in dimension 2\n\n# Geometric center\ncenter(X)         # (1.0, 0.0)\n\n# 1D projection onto a specific axis\nproj_x = projection(X, 1)  # interval(0.0, 2.0)","title":"2. Querying geometric properties"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#Point-containment-(in-/-)","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Check whether a point lies within a CartesianProduct:\n\n# In 1D:\nI = interval(0.0, 1.0)\n0.5 ∈ I           # true\n1.5 ∈ I           # false\n\n# In 2D (supports Tuples, SVector, and Vectors):\nX = interval(0.0, 1.0) × interval(0.0, 1.0)\n(0.5, 0.5) ∈ X    # true\n(1.2, 0.3) ∈ X    # false\n\n","title":"Point containment (in / ∈)"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#3.-Collapsed-and-lower-dimensional-geometries","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"A dimension is considered collapsed if its interval is degenerate (a = b). Bramble accurately tracks collapsed dimensions without heap allocations, enabling seamless modeling of lower-dimensional surfaces or interfaces embedded in higher-dimensional spaces:\n\n# 1D line embedded in 2D space: x ∈ [0, 1], y = 0\nline_in_2d = interval(0.0, 1.0) × point(0.0)\n\ndim(line_in_2d)       # 2 (spatial embedding dimension)\ntopo_dim(line_in_2d)  # 1 (topological dimension)\n\n# Check if individual dimensions are collapsed\nline_in_2d.collapsed[1]  # false (x-axis is extended)\nline_in_2d.collapsed[2]  # true  (y-axis is collapsed)\n\n","title":"3. Collapsed and lower-dimensional geometries"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#4.-Boundary-markers","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"PDE boundary conditions require tagging specific domain boundaries (e.g., Dirichlet, Neumann, Robin, inflow/outflow).","title":"4. Boundary markers"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#4.1-Boundary-symbol-conventions","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"For a D-dimensional domain, the standard boundary facets are:\n\n1D: :left, :right\n2D: :bottom, :top, :left, :right\n3D: :bottom, :top, :back, :front, :left, :right\n\nYou can inspect standard boundary symbols using get_boundary_symbols:\n\nget_boundary_symbols(2)\n# (:bottom, :top, :left, :right)","title":"4.1 Boundary symbol conventions"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#4.2-Creating-markers","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Markers are defined as :label => identifier pairs where identifier can be a single boundary symbol, a tuple of symbols, or a boolean function:\n\ngeom = interval(0.0, 5.0) × interval(0.0, 1.0)\n\n# 1. Using the markers() constructor\n# Define markers using pairs of :label => boundary_spec\nm1 = markers(\n    geom,\n    :inflow  => :left,\n    :outflow => :right,\n    :wall    => (:top, :bottom)\n)\n\n# Retrieve all defined labels\ncollect(labels(m1))\n# [:inflow, :outflow, :wall]","title":"4.2 Creating markers"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#4.3-Function-based-and-time-dependent-markers","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"You can also define internal or geometric subset markers using boolean condition functions, as well as time-dependent markers:\n\n# Condition-based marker: tag a subsection of the boundary or domain\nm_cond = markers(\n    geom,\n    :inflow    => :left,\n    :hot_spot  => (p -> p[1] > 2.5 && p[2] ≈ 0.0)\n)\n\n# Time-dependent markers:\ntime_span = interval(0.0, 10.0)\nm_time = markers(\n    geom,\n    time_span,\n    :moving_source => ((p, t) -> norm(p .- [t, 0.5]) < 0.2)\n)\n\n# Evaluate time-dependent markers at time t = 1.5\nm_evaluated = m_time(1.5)\n\n","title":"4.3 Function-based and time-dependent markers"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#5.-Computational-domains","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"A Domain joins a geometric set (CartesianProduct) with its boundary markers into a single unified object:\n\n# 1. Define geometry\ngeom = interval(0.0, 1.0) × interval(0.0, 1.0)\n\n# 2. Construct domain with inline boundary markers\nΩ = domain(\n    geom,\n    :dirichlet => (:left, :right),\n    :neumann   => (:top, :bottom)\n)\n\n# Or create a default domain marking all external boundaries as :boundary\nΩ_default = domain(geom)","title":"5. Computational domains"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#5.1-Domain-traits","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Domain automatically delegates geometric and marker methods directly:\n\ndim(Ω)            # 2\ntopo_dim(Ω)       # 2\ntails(Ω)          # ((0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0))\ncenter(Ω)         # (0.5, 0.5)\n(0.5, 0.5) ∈ Ω    # true\n\n# Access underlying set and markers\nset(Ω)            # CartesianProduct{2, Float64}\nmarkers(Ω)        # DomainMarkers\ncollect(labels(Ω)) # [:dirichlet, :neumann]\n\n","title":"5.1 Domain traits"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#6.-Practical-examples","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"","title":"6. Practical examples"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#Example-1:-1D-Rod-with-mixed-boundary-conditions","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Consider heat conduction along a 1D rod Omega = 0 L with L = 100, fixed temperature at x = 0 (:left) and insulated end at x = L (:right):\n\n(Image: 1D Rod Domain)\n\nL = 10.0\nrod_geom = interval(0.0, L)\n\n# Define domain with Dirichlet left boundary and Neumann right boundary\nrod = domain(\n    rod_geom,\n    :dirichlet => :left,\n    :neumann   => :right\n)\n\nprintln(\"Domain: \", rod)\nprintln(\"Dimension: \", dim(rod))\nprintln(\"Active Labels: \", collect(labels(rod)))\n\n","title":"Example 1: 1D Rod with mixed boundary conditions"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#Example-2:-2D-channel-flow-domain","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Consider fluid flow in a rectangular channel 0 5 times 0 1 with an inflow on the left, outflow on the right, and no-slip walls on top and bottom:\n\n(Image: 2D Channel Flow Domain)\n\nchannel_geom = interval(0.0, 5.0) × interval(0.0, 1.0)\n\nchannel = domain(\n    channel_geom,\n    :inflow  => :left,\n    :outflow => :right,\n    :wall    => (:top, :bottom)\n)\n\n@assert dim(channel) == 2\n@assert (2.5, 0.5) ∈ channel\nprintln(\"Channel labels: \", collect(labels(channel)))\n\n","title":"Example 2: 2D channel flow domain"},{"category":"section","location":"tutorials/geometry/#Example-3:-3D-heat-sink-domain","page":"Geometry Tutorial","text":"Consider heat dissipation across a 3D block 0 2 times 0 2 times 0 1 subjected to a bottom heat source, top convective cooling, and insulated lateral walls:\n\n(Image: 3D Heat Sink Domain)\n\nsink_geom = interval(0.0, 2.0) × interval(0.0, 2.0) × interval(0.0, 1.0)\n\nsink = domain(\n    sink_geom,\n    :heat_source => :bottom,\n    :convection  => :top,\n    :insulated   => (:left, :right, :front, :back)\n)\n\nprintln(\"3D Domain Center: \", center(sink))\nprintln(\"Active Labels: \", collect(labels(sink)))","title":"Example 3: 3D heat sink domain"},{"category":"section","location":"#Bramble.jl","page":"Home","text":"This documentation is for Bramble.jl, a Julia library implementing discretization methods to solve partial differential equations using finite differences on nonuniform grids.\n\nFor more information on the types of discretizations encompassed by Bramble.jl, please consult the papers\n\nJ. A. Ferreira and R. D. Grigorieff, On the supraconvergence of elliptic finite difference schemes, Applied Numerical Mathematics 28 (1998), pp. 275-292\nS. Barbeiro, J. A. Ferreira and R. D. Grigorieff, Supraconvergence of a finite difference scheme for solutions in H^s(0L), IMA Journal of Numerical Analysis 25.4 (2005), pp. 797–811\nJ. A. Ferreira and R. D. Grigorieff, Supraconvergence and Supercloseness of a Scheme for Elliptic Equations on Nonuniform Grids, Numerical Functional Analysis and Optimization 27.5-6 (2006), pp. 539–564","title":"Bramble.jl"}]
}
